Revision notes: Phase 4 was initially committed at 3989b12 (175 tests). A formal revision pass per the `before_completing_phases` protocol identified the following real code bugs and probe expectations needing correction:
- R1 (MAJOR): asof_join ShapeError when left frame collides with decision columns (`allowed`, `decision_code`) — collision detection only covered raw right columns, not evaluated decision columns; renamed with polars cross-join suffixes `_right` causing schema mismatch between joined groups and null groups.
- R4 (MAJOR): asof_join crashes when left frame has no `record_id` column (sort on `right_record_id` missing).
- R8 (MAJOR): Timing.__post_init__ only normalized non-datetime values; tz-aware datetimes stayed aware and crashed `decide()` comparisons.
- R3, R7, R10: probe expectation errors (wrong expectation about null-row column retention, 0-row frame broadcast, NaN digest equality) — code was correct.
- Additional fixes from the second independent pass: collision-safe rename map (`_right_rename_map`) with deduped universe to prevent DuplicateError when a decision-named column (e.g. `allowed`) exists on both raw right and the engine-decision columns; always-include right record_id in tie_cols to preserve largest-record_id determinism even without a left record_id; empty-right null-join now uses the same `_right_side_schema` as the no-qualifying path (no silent column destruction); `normalize_instant` now handles Z-suffix ISO strings and raises clean TypeError on bad types; `Timing.__post_init__` coerce plain-string `publication_precision` to enum and parse string `vintage_date` to date; null `publication_precision` conservatively treated as DATE (next-day availability) preventing a temporal look-ahead leak.
